# Profiling reports

Profiling outputs are persisted as JSON rather than existing only as console output.

Current expected report structure:

```{text}
reports/
└── profiling/
    ├── lor_profile.json
    ├── icon_grid_profile.json
    ├── icon_t2m_<run>.json
    ├── icon_plr_bridge_profile.json
    └── afs_population_profile.json
```

This provides both:

- human-inspectable output
- machine-readable records that can later be surfaced through an orchestrator or monitoring layer

Architecture 1 intentionally avoids introducing a separate profiling framework. The scripts and JSON files make the behavior directly visible to a reviewer.
